      "message": "2. Install Certificate File On BMC — IPv6 branch captures cert_id only on HTTP_CREATED or HTTP_OK, but cert_id is unset on other status codes before Delete All Sessions is called (lib/certificate_utils.robot)\n\nIn the IPv6 ELSE branch, Delete All Sessions is called before the cert_id IF/ELSE block is resolved for the status \u003d\u003d \u0027ok\u0027 assertion. If the status check fails mid-way, the session is already deleted, which is fine — but cert_id is set to -1 only inside a nested IF. If the compiler evaluates both conditions as false (e.g. neither HTTP_CREATED nor HTTP_OK), cert_id is never set, yet it is RETURN\u0027d. This will cause a variable-not-set runtime error. The IPv4 branch handles this safely; the IPv6 branch should mirror it exactly.",
