      "side": 1,
      "message": "🔴 Critical / Must-fix\n1. Delete Certificate Via BMC CLI — existence-check logic broken (lib/certificate_utils.robot, diff lines ~224–234)\n\nThe patch comments out the file-existence check:\n\n#${file_status}  ${stderr}  ${rc}\u003d  BMC Execute Command\n#...  [ -f ${certificate_file_path} ] \u0026\u0026 echo \"Found\" || echo \"Not Found\"\n#IF  \"${file_status}\" !\u003d \"Found\"  RETURN\nBMC Execute Command  rm ${certificate_file_path}\n\nThis removes the guard that prevents rm from running when no certificate exists. Now rm will be executed unconditionally. If the file is absent, rm will error and the keyword will fail where it previously returned cleanly. This is a regression that affects every caller of Delete Certificate Via BMC CLI, not just the IPv6 paths. The commented-out code should be restored or replaced with a proper fix — not left as dead comments.",
